    "title": "Tompkins County Public Library to host series on US Constitution - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By WSKG ,\n7 hours ago The Tompkins County Public Library is hosting a new series called “The Constitution: Rights to Know.”. The four-part program, led by local legal experts, will cover the Bill of Rights, voting, citizenship, and immigration. It will run through the end of 2025, with a discussion scheduled each month. The... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
